.TH NAMGEN 1 "2026" "namgen" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
namgen \- Flexible name generator and procedural fantasy/sci-fi name generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B namgen
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B namgen
generates names by combining adjectives and nouns with configurable casing and separators, or using built-in procedural name generators for fantasy and science fiction universes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-adj\-file FILE
Path to custom adjectives file
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-exclude STRING
Characters to strip from generated words (default: hyphen, apostrophe)
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-noun\-file FILE
Path to custom noun file
.TP
.B \-s SEP, \-\-separator SEP
Custom separator string (default: \-)
.TP
.B \-x, \-\-null\-separator
Do not print the separator (concatenates words)
.TP
.B \-c COUNT, \-\-count COUNT
Number of names to generate (default: terminal height)
.TP
.B \-S NUM, \-\-seed NUM
Seed random number generator deterministically for reproducible runs
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-unique
Ensure no duplicate names are emitted in the generated batch
.TP
.B \-m REGEX, \-\-match REGEX
Filter generated names by regular expression pattern
.TP
.B \-\-min\-len NUM
Minimum character length constraint for generated names
.TP
.B \-\-max\-len NUM
Maximum character length constraint for generated names
.TP
.B \-\-syllables RANGE
Constraint syllable count (e.g. 2 or 2-3)
.TP
.B \-\-alliterate
Filter for alliterative multi-word names
.TP
.B \-\-with\-lore, \-\-meaning
Append procedural lore epithet and etymological meaning
.TP
.B \-\-markov [GEN]
Generate novel names using character n-gram Markov model trained on generator
.TP
.B \-\-order NUM
N-gram order for Markov synthesizer (default: 3)
.TP
.B \-\-train FILE
Train Markov synthesizer from external text corpus
.TP
.B \-\-synthesize COUNT
Synthesize novel names from trained Markov model
.TP
.B \-\-find KEYWORD
Search available generators matching keyword/pattern
.TP
.B \-\-serve [ADDR:PORT]
Run embedded zero-dependency HTTP REST daemon (default: 127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-
Stream standard input line-by-line through casing/formatting pipeline
.TP
.B \-\-color[=WHEN]
Colorize output (auto, always, never; default: auto)
.TP
.B \-\-compose GEN1,GEN2
Compose multiple generators together in a structured format
.TP
.B \-\-template STRING
Template format string for generator composition (default: "{1} of {2}")
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Launch full-screen interactive terminal explorer UI with live search and preview
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results as a JSON array of strings
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Output results as CSV format with header
.TP
.B \-\-slug, \-\-kebab
Convert output names to lowercase kebab-case URL slugs
.TP
.B \-\-cap, \-\-capcasing
Capitalize first letter of both adjective and noun
.TP
.B \-\-camel, \-\-camelcasing
CamelCase style (adjective lower-cased, noun capitalized)
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-elf, \-\-lotr\-elf, \-\-lord_of_the_rings\-elfs
Generate Lord of the Rings elf style names
.TP
